ring%20at%20elevated%20levels.%20But%20the%20population%20holding%20multiple%20jobs%20looks%20different%20from%20before%20the%20pandemic%2C%20with%20a%20growing%20cohort%20of%20more%20traditionally%20stable%20Americans%20now%20seeking%20multiple%20income%20streams.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20second%20job%20is%20no%20longer%20just%20a%20survival%20tactic%20for%20the%20lowest%20earners%2C%20or%20a%20nice%20income%20boost%20for%20the%20highest%20earners%20%E2%80%94%20it's%20increasingly%20showing%20up%20for%20college-educated%2C%20middle-income%20Americans%20and%20the%20women%20of%20the%20workforce%2C%20who%20seem%20to%20be%20seeking%20out%20an%20extra%20buffer%20of%20stability%20and%20income.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAn%20analysis%20from%20the%20Richmond%20Federal%20Reserve%20found%20that%20before%20the%20pandemic%2C%20the%20share%20of%20multiple%20jobholders%20across%20income%20groups%20was%20similar%3A%20low-%2C%20middle-%2C%20and%20high-earners%20worked%20multiple%20jobs%20in%20roughly%20equal%20proportion.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20the%20past%20few%20years%2C%20that's%20changed.%20Middle-income%20earners%20are%20much%20more%20likely%20to%20hold%20multiple%20jobs%20than%20their%20lower-earning%20counterparts%2C%20and%20sit%20just%20barely%20below%20their%20higher-earning%20peers.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAt%20the%20same%20time%2C%20college-educated%20workers%20have%20increasingly%20been%20creeping%20into%20the%20multiple%20jobholder%20workforce.%20In%20the%201990s%2C%20they%20made%20up%20around%2035%25%20of%20those%20holding%20multiple%20jobs%3B%20by%202024%2C%20they%20made%20up%20over%20half%2C%20according%20to%20the%20Richmond%20Fed%20analysis.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESimultaneously%2C%20the%20number%20of%20women%20holding%20multiple%20jobs%20has%20increased%20in%20the%20last%20few%20years%2C%20according%20to%20the%20Bureau%20of%20Labor%20Statistics's%20latest%20employment%20data.%20The%20gender%20gap%20in%20multiple%20jobholding%20has%20widened%2C%20meaning%20that%20more%20women%20%E2%80%94%20especially%20those%20aged%2020%20to%2024%20%E2%80%94%20are%20working%20in%20several%20roles.%20That%20tracks%20with%20a%20labor%20force%20where%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwomen-outnumber-men-in-the-college-educated-american-workforce-2019-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ewomen%20have%20outnumbered%20men%3C%2Fa%3E%20with%20college%20degrees%2C%20and%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgen-z-millennial-women-earn-more-than-men-16-cities-2022-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eyounger%20women%20in%20some%20areas%3C%2Fa%3E%20earn%20more%20than%20their%20male%20counterparts.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%20data-script%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdatawrapper.dwcdn.net%2FX7AFD%2Fembed.js%5C%22%20data-styles%3D%5C%22default-width%5C%22%20data-embed-type%3D%5C%22custom%5C%22%20data-type%3D%5C%22embed%5C%22%3E%3Cdiv%3E%3Cdiv%20class%3D%5C%22feedlyNoScript%5C%22%3E%3Cimg%20alt%3D%5C%22Line%20chart%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdatawrapper.dwcdn.net%2FX7AFD%2Ffull.png%5C%22%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3Cp%3ETaken%20together%2C%20the%20data%20indicate%20that%20more%20educated%20and%20traditionally%20more%20affluent%20Americans%20feel%20an%20urge%20to%20bring%20in%20multiple%20income%20streams.%20Side%20hustles%20are%20increasingly%20prevalent%20across%20the%20economy%3A%20The%20share%20of%20Americans%20holding%20down%20a%20side%20hustle%20has%20increased%20from%2019%25%20in%202017%20to%2027%25%20in%202025%2C%20per%20a%20Bankrate%20survey.%20Official%20measures%20of%20multiple%20jobholding%20also%20often%20fail%20to%20completely%20capture%20the%20number%20of%20workers%20participating%20in%20gig%20work%2C%20since%20BLS's%20rate%20measures%20workers%20who%20hold%20at%20least%20one%20traditional%20wage%20job.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAnd%20that%20might%20show%20how%20workers%20feel%20about%20their%20prospects.%20Women%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Ffred.stlouisfed.org%2Fseries%2FLNS12000002%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%